      "dom_id": "question-175527",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "$2$ is odd **and** $3$ is prime.\n\nConsider the compound statement above and the following notations:\n\n- $P: \\textrm{$2$ is odd}$\n\n- $Q: \\textrm{$3$ is prime}$",
      "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land$\".\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n\\[\n\\underbrace{2 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is odd} }_P \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \\underbrace{3 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is prime} }_Q,\n\\]\n\nthat is, $P \\land Q.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
