      "problem": "$2+3$ equals $5$ **or** $\\pi$ is rational.\n\nConsider the compound statement above and the following notations:\n\n- $A: \\textrm{$2+3$ equals $5$}$\n\n- $B: \\textrm{$\\pi$ is rational}$",
      "worked_solution": "The word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor$\".\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n\\[\n\\underbrace{2+3 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ equals }\\vphantom{p} 5 }_A \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \n\\underbrace{\\pi \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is rational} }_B,\n\\]\n\nthat is, $A \\lor B.$",
