      "name": null,
      "problem": "$6$ is a composite number **and** $2$ is negative.\n\nConsider the compound statement above and the following notations:\n\n- $R: \\textrm{$6$ is a composite number}$\n\n- $S: \\textrm{$2$ is negative}$",
      "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land$\".\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n\\[\n\\underbrace{6 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is a composite number} }_R \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \n\\underbrace{2 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is negative} }_S,\n\\]\n\nthat is, $R \\land S.$",
