      "raw_html": "<div class=\"question\" id=\"question-178520\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">7.</span><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"178520\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><blockquote>\n<p>$9$ is a perfect square, <strong>or</strong> $ 3 \\geq 4$ <strong>or</strong> $ 3= 5-1.$</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Express the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>$P: \\textrm{$9$ is a perfect square}$ </p>\n</li>\n<li><p>$Q: \\textrm{$3 \\geq 4$}$</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>$R: \\textrm{$3=5-1$}$</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyEasy\">E</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Tue, Oct 13th @ 11:08 AM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:14</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: red;\">Incorrect</span></span></div></div>"
    },
    {
      "dom_id": "question-177717",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "$6|10$ **and** $6|18,$ **or** $11$ is prime **and** odd.\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $M: \\textrm{$6|10$}$\n\n- $P: \\textrm{$6|18$}$\n\n- $N: \\textrm{$11$ is prime}$\n\n- $Q: \\textrm{$11$ is odd}$",
      "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $6|10$ and $6|18.$ This corresponds to\n\\[\n\\underbrace{6|10}_M \\quad \n\\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \n\\underbrace{6|18}_P\n\\]\nthat is, $M \\land P.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $11$ is prime and odd. This corresponds to\n\\[\n\\underbrace{11 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is prime}}_N \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \n\\underbrace{11 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is odd }}_Q,\n\\]\nthat is, $N \\land Q.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\\[\n\\underbrace{6|10 \\textbf{ and } 6|18}_{M \\, \\land \\, P} \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \n\\underbrace{11 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is prime } \\textbf{and} \\textrm{ odd }}_{N \\, \\land \\, Q},\n\\]\nthat is, $(M \\land P) \\lor (N \\land Q).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "problem_field_keys": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Correct",
      "proof_feedback": null,
      "html": "<div id=\"question-177717\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">8.</span><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"177717\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><blockquote>\n<p>$6|10$ <strong>and</strong> $6|18,$ <strong>or</strong> $11$ is prime <strong>and</strong> odd.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Express the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>$M: \\textrm{$6|10$}$</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>$P: \\textrm{$6|18$}$</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>$N: \\textrm{$11$ is prime}$ </p>\n</li>\n<li><p>$Q: \\textrm{$11$ is odd}$</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyModerate\">M</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Tue, Oct 13th @ 11:08 AM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:15</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: green;\">Correct</span></span></div></div>",
