      "raw_html": "<div class=\"question\" id=\"question-177717\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">8.</span><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"177717\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><blockquote>\n<p>$6|10$ <strong>and</strong> $6|18,$ <strong>or</strong> $11$ is prime <strong>and</strong> odd.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Express the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>$M: \\textrm{$6|10$}$</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>$P: \\textrm{$6|18$}$</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>$N: \\textrm{$11$ is prime}$ </p>\n</li>\n<li><p>$Q: \\textrm{$11$ is odd}$</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyModerate\">M</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Tue, Oct 13th @ 11:08 AM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:15</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: green;\">Correct</span></span></div></div>"
    },
    {
      "dom_id": "question-178524",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "$6 \\leq 3^2$ **and** $6$ is even, **and** $13$ is a prime number.\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P: \\textrm{$6 \\leq 3^2$}$\n\n- $Q: \\textrm{$6$ is even}$\n\n- $R: \\textrm{$13$ is a prime number}$",
      "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $6 \\leq 3^2$ and $6$ is even. This corresponds to\n\\[\n\\underbrace{6 \\leq 3^2}_P \\quad \n\\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \n\\underbrace{6 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is even} }_Q,\n\\]\nthat is, $P \\land Q.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $13$ is a prime number. This corresponds to $R.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\\[\n\\underbrace{6 \\leq 3^2 \\textbf{ and } 6 \\textrm{ is even } }_{P \\, \\land \\, Q}, \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \n\\underbrace{13 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is a prime number} }_R \n\\]\nthat is, $(P \\land Q) \\land R.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "problem_field_keys": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Incorrect",
      "proof_feedback": null,
      "html": "<div id=\"question-178524\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">9.</span><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"178524\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><blockquote>\n<p>$6 \\leq 3^2$ <strong>and</strong> $6$ is even, <strong>and</strong> $13$ is a prime number.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Express the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>$P: \\textrm{$6 \\leq 3^2$}$</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>$Q: \\textrm{$6$ is even}$</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>$R: \\textrm{$13$ is a prime number}$ </p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyEasy\">E</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Tue, Oct 13th @ 11:09 AM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:17</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: red;\">Incorrect</span></span></div></div>",
