      "raw_html": "<div class=\"question\" id=\"question-178524\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">9.</span><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"178524\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><blockquote>\n<p>$6 \\leq 3^2$ <strong>and</strong> $6$ is even, <strong>and</strong> $13$ is a prime number.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Express the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>$P: \\textrm{$6 \\leq 3^2$}$</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>$Q: \\textrm{$6$ is even}$</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>$R: \\textrm{$13$ is a prime number}$ </p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyEasy\">E</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Tue, Oct 13th @ 11:09 AM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:17</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: red;\">Incorrect</span></span></div></div>"
    },
    {
      "dom_id": "question-177457",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "$4$ is even **or** $4^2=12$, **and** $-2$ is an integer number.\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $M: \\textrm{$4$ is even}$\n\n- $N: \\textrm{$4^2=12$}$\n\n- $P: \\textrm{$-2$ is an integer number}$",
      "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $4$ is even or $4^2=12.$ This corresponds to\n\\[\n\\underbrace{4 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is even }}_M \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \\underbrace{4^2=12 }_N,\n\\]\nthat is, $M \\lor N.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $-2$ is an integer number. This corresponds to $P.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\\[\n\n\\underbrace{4 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is even} \\textbf{ or } \\vphantom{p} 4^2=12}_{M \\, \\lor \\, N}, \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \n\\underbrace{-2 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is an integer number} }_P \n\\]\n\nthat is, $(M \\lor N) \\land P.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "problem_field_keys": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Correct",
      "proof_feedback": null,
      "html": "<div id=\"question-177457\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">10.</span><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"177457\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><blockquote>\n<p>$4$ is even <strong>or</strong> $4^2=12$, <strong>and</strong> $-2$ is an integer number.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Express the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>$M: \\textrm{$4$ is even}$ </p>\n</li>\n<li><p>$N: \\textrm{$4^2=12$}$</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>$P: \\textrm{$-2$ is an integer number}$</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyEasy\">E</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Tue, Oct 13th @ 11:09 AM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:14</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: green;\">Correct</span></span></div></div>",
