    {
      "dom_id": "question-175916",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "\\[\n\\underbrace{0.33 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is rational} }_A \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \\underbrace{3+1= 2+2}_B\n\\]\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(\\land)$ and \"or\" $(\\lor)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A \\land B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A \\lor B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is true, and $B$ is true. Therefore, the result is true:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\underbrace{0.33 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is rational} }_A \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \n\\underbrace{3+1= 2+2 }_B\n&\\:\\:\\equiv\\: \\text{true} \\land \\textrm{true} \\equiv \\textrm{true}\n\\end{align*}",
