      "dom_id": "question-175917",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "\\[\n\\underbrace{\\{1, 2\\}\\cap \\{3\\}=\\{1,2,3\\}}_A \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \\underbrace{9 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is prime}}_B\n\\]\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(\\land)$ and \"or\" $(\\lor)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A \\land B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A \\lor B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is false, and $B$ is false. Therefore, the result is false:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\underbrace{\\{1, 2\\}\\cap \\{3\\}=\\{1,2,3\\}}_A \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \n\\underbrace{9 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is prime}}_B\n&\\:\\:\\equiv\\: \\text{false} \\land \\textrm{false} \\equiv \\textrm{false}\n\\end{align*}",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
