      "raw_html": "<div class=\"question\" id=\"question-175930\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">18.</span><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"175930\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>\\[\n\\underbrace{\\overbrace{\\{1,2\\}\\cup\\{2\\}=\\{1,2\\}}^P \n\\quad \\overbrace{\\vphantom{|}\\textbf{or}}^{\\lor} \\quad \n\\overbrace{11\\vphantom{|}\\textrm{ is prime} }^Q }_{P \\, \\lor \\, Q} \n\\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{|}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \n\\underbrace{2 \\vphantom{|}\\textrm{ is a perfect square} }_R \n\\]</p>\n<p>For the compound statement above, we have that</p>\n</div><div class=\"questionBody\" id=\"questionBody-175930\"></div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyEasy\">E</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Tue, Oct 13th @ 11:13 AM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:29</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: red;\">Incorrect</span></span></div></div>"
    },
    {
      "dom_id": "question-178160",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "\\[\n\\underbrace{\\{1,2\\}\\cup\\{3\\}=\\{1,2,3\\}}_P \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{|}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land}\\quad \n\\underbrace{ \\overbrace{0 \\in \\mathbb{Z}}^Q \n\\quad \\overbrace{\\vphantom{|}\\textbf{and}}^{\\land} \\quad \n\\overbrace{1 \\vphantom{|}\\textrm{ is positive}}^R }_{Q \\, \\land \\, R}\n\\]\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(\\land)$ and \"or\" $(\\lor)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A \\land B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A \\lor B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is true, $Q$ is true, and $R$ is true. Therefore, $Q \\land R$ is true, and the result is true:\n\\begin{align*}\nP \\land (Q\\land R) \n&\\equiv\\text{true} \\land \\overbrace{(\\textrm{true} \\land \\textrm{true})}^{\\textrm{true}} \\\\[5pt]\n&\\equiv \\textrm{true} \\land \\textrm{true} \\\\[3pt]\n&\\equiv\\textrm{true}\n\\end{align*}",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "problem_field_keys": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Correct",
      "proof_feedback": null,
      "html": "<div id=\"question-178160\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">19.</span><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"178160\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>\\[\n\\underbrace{\\{1,2\\}\\cup\\{3\\}=\\{1,2,3\\}}_P \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{|}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land}\\quad \n\\underbrace{ \\overbrace{0 \\in \\mathbb{Z}}^Q \n\\quad \\overbrace{\\vphantom{|}\\textbf{and}}^{\\land} \\quad \n\\overbrace{1 \\vphantom{|}\\textrm{ is positive}}^R }_{Q \\, \\land \\, R}\n\\]</p>\n<p>For the compound statement above, we have that</p>\n</div><div id=\"questionBody-178160\" class=\"questionBody\"></div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyEasy\">E</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Tue, Oct 13th @ 11:14 AM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:26</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: green;\">Correct</span></span></div></div>",
