      "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14181557/observations/lesson-step-153501-b8171cde8d4b1db79595.html",
      "screenshot": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14181557/observations/lesson-step-153501-b8171cde8d4b1db79595.png",
      "source_url": "https://mathacademy.com/topics/60",
      "captured_at": 1791915379.0652704,
      "math_academy_id": 8142,
      "title": "Truth Values of Statements Containing the \"And\" Connective",
      "content": "Let's now consider the truth values of the logical connector \"and\". We have the following key idea:\n\n*The statement $A \\land B$ is true if $A$ is true **and** $B$ is true. Otherwise, it is false.* \n\nLet's determine the truth values of the following compound statement:\n\n$2$ is positive **and** $2$ is even.\n\nWriting this in symbols, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{2\\text{ is positive}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{2\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nor, simply\n\n$$\nA\\land B.\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is true and $B$ is true, this compound statement is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∧B≡\\text{true}∧\\text{true}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this context, the symbol \"$\\equiv$\" means \"is logically equivalent to.\" \n\nLet's now consider a similar compound statement but with the $2$ replaced with a $3$ in the second statement.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{2\\text{ is positive}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{3\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can write this symbolically as follows:\n\n$$\nA\\land C\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is true and $C$ is false, this compound statement is false:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∧C≡\\text{true}∧\\text{false}≡\\text{false}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
    {
      "dom_id": "step-153502",
      "name": "Truth Values of Statements Containing the \"Or\" Connective",
      "problem": "Let's now consider the truth values of the logical connector \"or\". We have the following key idea:\n\n*The statement $A \\lor B$ is true if $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or both $A$ and $B$ are true. Otherwise, it is false.* \n\nLet's consider some examples:\n\n- First, consider the following statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{2\\text{ is positive}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{2\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is true and $B$ is true, this compound statement is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∨B≡\\text{true}∨\\text{true}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, consider the following statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{2\\text{ is positive}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{3\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is true, this compound statement is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∨C≡\\text{true}∨\\text{false}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Now, consider the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{-2\\text{ is positive}}_{⏟}}_{D}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{2\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $B$ is true, this compound statement is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D∨B≡\\text{false}∨\\text{true}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, consider the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{-2\\text{ is positive}}_{⏟}}_{D}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{3\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $D$ and $C$ are both false, this compound statement is false:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D∨C≡\\text{false}∨\\text{false}≡\\text{false}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
